cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you cite this verification artifact, please cite the specific archived version you
  checked, not the repository in general. Each release has its own version DOI; see the
  "Archival" section in README.md.
title: >-
  convex-uniform-honeycombs: machine-checked companion to "The 28 convex uniform
  honeycombs: a completeness theorem"
abstract: >-
  The verification artifact for the paper's claims: the Alphabet Theorem (only 13 cells can
  occur in any face-to-face unit-edge honeycomb by convex uniform polyhedra) via an
  interval-certified corona fixpoint, two exact identities over Q(sqrt 5), closed forms and
  an interleaving lemma closing the prism and antiprism tails with no cap anywhere, and
  lifted odd-face walks killing the nine exotic prism families; the species table of exactly
  34 vertex stars, enumerated as edge-to-edge tilings of the sphere of directions, with the
  Barlow fcc/hcp dichotomy as a corollary; the mono-species shell filter cutting 34 to 26;
  the transitive pattern enumeration landing on exactly 28 fingerprint classes, including
  the collision that shows local consistency does not imply developability; the completeness
  audit (periodization, coherence, separation, cap closure); the re-verification in exact arithmetic over Q(sqrt 2, sqrt 3) of
  all 34 star models, all 28 periodization certificates, the coherence of every accepted pattern
  with its class (within the caps and, on the ten skeletons germ forcing leaves open, beyond
  them) and germ forcing on every skeleton — every positive certificate on the critical path;
  the identification against the classical list of Grunbaum and Deza-Shtogrin; and the
  appendix's independent Delaney-Dress symbol census, which reproduces the count 28 sharing
  only the species table with the proof. The whole artifact re-derives from scratch in a few
  minutes, the exact replay pattern by pattern opt-in; all shared machinery is the pinned
  research-core library.
